/-! ## Validation of the Secp256k1 axioms.

    Two things are checked here.

    First, the axioms that talk about the builtins are sampled on the vectors of the Plutus
    conformance suite, under
    `test-cases/uplc/evaluation/builtin/semantics/verifyEcdsaSecp256k1Signature/` and
    `.../verifySchnorrSecp256k1Signature/`.  `opaque` definitions still compile, so `#guard`
    runs the real builtins; the result is read through `Except.toOption`, which is the
    `.error`/`.ok b` distinction the axioms are phrased in and is insensitive to the wording
    of the error message.

    Second, the axiom set is shown to be satisfiable, by exhibiting a model of `AllSpec`.
    This is the Lean counterpart of the `#blaster ... → False` probes: those ask Z3 for a
    model, which it does not manage to build once the constraint ties the result of an
    uninterpreted function to the *lengths* of its arguments. -/

/-! ### ECDSA vectors

